A||N||14||DKOV||Good Turbo Question!||||1||
Z||000000||DKOV||12-20-2001||02:10 PM||||I just thought of something...<P>In 1990, I briefly owned a Black Grand Prix GTP with a Turbo Charged 3.1L.  It only put out 205 HP under boost.  Wasn't the 3.1L around 185 HP stock?<P>Anyway, How hard do you suppose it would be to adapt the 3.1L Turbo, that alread has all the proper fittings and sensors and stuff, to the 3.4L?<P>That Turbo could not have been putting out THAT much boost to generate only 20 HP or so...  I wonder if it would even be worth it.<P>Just a thought   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000001||DKOV||12-20-2001||02:14 PM||||OK... I see that the consensus is the 3.1L put out about 160 HP stock, not 185.<P>So that would mean the Turbo was putting out around 45 HP at boost.  That's a little better I suppose.<P>Still, is it possible or even worth it?<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||12-20-2001||03:32 PM||||I think the 3.1 turbo was 225, vs 160 for the N/A version.<BR>The turbo 3.1 had the Gen II heads. For various reasons, adapting those for use in the Fiero is a good bit of work.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DKOV||12-20-2001||03:54 PM||||I got the specs on the 3.1L Turbo here and they say 205...  I wish it were 225   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The Gen II heads?  Aren't they similar in exit porting to the exhaust as the 3.4L TDC?<P>Getting in the piping is mostly what I am thinking about.  The TDC motor is a very good breather on its own, but mine is also ported and polished all around.<P>If 160 HP was the base and 205 was the Turbo HP... that's an increase of about 22% or so.  If it were 225, then the increase is more like 29%<P>So, if mated to the 3.4L TDC at the 22% then base HP would increase to 262.3 HP.  That's not bad...<P>Considering the mods to my motor and the current HP, which is well above that figure...  Would the increase apply to the modified HP or degrade some percentage as applied to the new total modified HP?<P>In other words, If I were putting out around say... 300HP and I added the Turbo and actually seen a 22% increase from the Turbo itself, would it be 300HP + 22% or would it be more like 215HP + 22% + HP increased from mods?<P>Does that make sense?<P>The reason for asking is this...  My Supercharger on my Durango R/T shows an increase in HP described as the % increase over STOCK HP.  Is that percentage constant or is it averaged DOWN when totalled in with other mods.<P>245 Base HP + 45% increase from SC is 355 HP<P>Adding Headers that provide another 10.2 % HP or 25 +/- HP is calculated from BASE HP? or is that from the NEW total after the SC was added?<P>If so, that would be a completely different number!<P>Base HP addition would total only (245 + 10.2%) 380 HP<P>whereas<P>SC HP plus the Headers would total (355HP + 10.2%) 391 HP, an additional 11 HP.<P>Okay... my brain hurts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shaun41178||12-20-2001||04:53 PM||||The turbo in the turbo GP would be too small.  Wonder why it only made 45 more hp then a stock 3.1?  Well for one they kept the boost down.  Second the turbo was smaller then my wang and believe me that is saying something.<P>I think the turbo was a t-25.  Dkov if you were going to use this turbo on your TDC I would not  recommend it.  its too small.  it was too small for the 3.1 and your 3.4 breathes a hell of a lot better<P>As to your question about the exhaust ports lining up, I dont know.  good way to check would be to look at a set of iron heads and find out.  Yes I know you might think that sounds dumb but the Gen 2 heads and the fiero iron heads have the same exhaust port location and shape.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierobsessed||12-20-2001||10:18 PM||||well, Ill let the picture speak for itself. too bad that the guy wouldnt sell me his 3.1 turbo GP <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/nstarfiero/31.jpg">  <BR>||||reg||14
Z||000006||DRH||12-20-2001||11:30 PM||||I agree with Shaun, the T25 is way too small for a 3.4 DOHC. A lot of TGP people seem to think it's too small for their 3.1.<P>An engines power is determined to a large extent by how much air you can move in and out. A 4 valve/cylinder DOHC has a LOT more ability for flow than a 2 valve OHV. If the turbo is too small it won't be able to hold the desired boost pressure at high RPM.<P>It's more complicated than just finding a percentage increase, especially when you're going between engines with such different characteristics. It may or may not have the same effect on the other engine. <P>You also need to look at the whole power band and decide exactly what you're looking to get. With a DOHC you could put a huge turbo and intercooler on it and get some really impressive numbers at high RPM but have nothing below 4000 or so. You could put a small one on and get some help from the quick spool up at the low end but have it quit pulling at the upper end.<P>I'm thinking of doing a turbo one of these days on a DOHC. Preliminary research looks like a T3/T4 hybrid might make a good compromise of power and driveability.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||00lE||12-21-2001||05:22 AM||||The Turbo Grand Prix 3.1 VIN V is basically  just a stock 3.1 VIN T with a turbocharger system installed.  The 3.1 VIN T was rated at <B>140hp @ 4800 rpm</B> and 180 ft-lbs @ 3600 rpm.  As others stated above, the turbocharger brought the horsepower for the TGP up to 205 @ 5200 rpm and the torque to 225 ft-lbs @ 2100 rpm.  That is a peak increase of <B>65 hp</B>.  The TGP's limited max boost can also be increased via eprom code to obtain even better performance.<P>The hp of the NA 3.1 VIN T's never increased above 140. In 1994, the engine was redesigned and redesignated as the 3100 VIN M.  The first 3100's produced were only rated at 155 hp, but by late 1999 it was capable of 175 hp @ 5200 rpm (only 5hp less than the 3400).||||reg||1
Z||000008||artherd||12-21-2001||06:20 AM||||DKOV- I just wouldn't bother, buddy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>To be honest, that little turbo slaped onto your monster motor would probally suck horsepower FROM your engine.  It'd act like a LeMans flow-restrictor plate. Never pumping in enough air for you, even at insane turbine speeds.  Then it will heat the charge and blow your high-compression motor  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you really want to turbo your motor, you're going to need to tear it down and build it back up for turbo use.  This means an 8.5:1 compression ratio MAX.  Then run something like a T4 or T3/T4 hybrid, with wastegate and BOV, all controled by custom electronics (Electromotive) programmed by a profesional.<P>You may get 400hp out of a setup like this (WCF aparently does!) But it will cost a fortune, and I belive you're making 300hp now?<P>It will never have the tuned explosive feel and quality of your Lotous. Though it will out-run it.<P>It will also radically alter the character of your engine, if you LIKE the N/A 7-grand screamer, I'd say stick with it!<P>Take the money and get fully ajustable Held Motorsports coilover front and rear springs/suspension with rod-ends  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>PS: I'd calculate HP numbers on a dyno, after a certin point, the 'math' just blows up and starts to mean nothing.  I figure I'll be getting ~325hp out of my stock (counting little boosts for exhaust and aftermarket management being supior to stock.) but hell if I'll know what it's making until I throw it all in and get on those roolers!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000009||DKOV||12-21-2001||02:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>DKOV- I just wouldn't bother, buddy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>...<P>Take the money and get fully ajustable Held Motorsports coilover front and rear springs/suspension with rod-ends   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was just curious.  Why nobody was talking about this motor.  Why nobody was thinking about swiping that Turbo.  Why nobody ever even asked about it...  I guess I know now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>AS for the Held wide-track...  WAY ahead of ya buddy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>You and I...  and our 3.4s...  we've GOT to get together someday!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000010||00lE||12-21-2001||08:57 PM||||Actually, questions concerning the use of the TGP 3.1 motor in the Fiero have come up quite frequently on this board.<P>TGP parts seem to command a high premium, since many believe it to be a collectable car. LOL  In real life, the only item that is of high value from the TGP for Fiero turbo applications would be the eprom code, since it was co-designed by McLaren.  The rest of the turbo system can quite easily be duplicated and improved upon.<P>The TGP turbocharger is indeed much too small for application on the 3.4 DOHC.  It is however, about the right size for boosting a stock Fiero 2.8<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cooter||12-21-2001||09:27 PM||||I have that file, but screwed up the prom- hey, at least I was smart enough to save the code before I went stupid   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>edit: I found the prom and it is NOT the one I screwed up. I also have the '727 ecm for it too. Keep in mind, this is a DIS motor. <p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 12-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||00lE||12-21-2001||11:07 PM||||You can get a copy of the TGP eprom code for free, it is available on the DIY-EFI ftp site:<P>ftp://ftp.diy-efi.org/pub/gmecm/bin_lib/<P>(Look under the /1227727/8F 5F/ directory, the 8F Program ID, BCC = AUAF)  The file name is AUAF.BIN<P>The code will work on the 1227727 or 1227730 PCM, but you need to burn it to a 6 cyl memcal.  Any common MPFI VIN T 3.1 memcal will work just fine, and they an not hard to find at all, just about any salvage yard should be overflowing with them.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Note : Use an FTP Client software package to access the site, most web browser's have problems with the way the site is setup..<p>[This message has been edited by 00lE (edited 12-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Fierobsessed||12-22-2001||12:06 PM||||What kind of map sensor would I have to use If I wanted to boost my 3.1 DIS, Who has it? What does it cost? and does It have to be wired in or plugged in or do I need a new computer? That is my engine that is pictured above.<P>------------------<BR>Matt D<BR>1984 Indy Fiero (auto)<BR>1985 2m4 V6 DIS 3.1 Auto||||reg||1
Z||000014||00lE||12-22-2001||08:24 PM||||GM part #16254539  ($32.15 at gmpartsdirect.com)<P>Its a 2 bar MAP sensor that simply replaces the existing 1 bar map sensor (externally identical), just a couple screws.<P>If you are using DIS with a stock 3.1 PCM, then you are already using a PCM that will run TGP code.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 00lE (edited 12-22-2001).]||||reg||1
